# Regexes exempt from tools/check-secrets.sh, one per line.
#
# Unlike .secretwords, this file is tracked, so CI enforces the same list.
# That is the point. A list of allowed things is not itself sensitive.
#
# Keep entries tight. Exempt the exact line shape that trips the gate, never
# the pattern in general, or the gate stops earning its keep.

# z390 writes its own version and the JVM's into every listing header. Both
# are dotted numbers, and z390's has four parts, so the IPv4 rule bites.
USING z390 [0-9.]+ ON J2SE [0-9.]+
